A324109	filfix	0	new A005940()	Also J070776 is a subsequence. This follows because for every n of the form 2^i * p^j (where p is an odd prime, and i >= 0, j >= 0), we have €324108(2^i * p^j) = J324054(2^i - 1)*J324054(p^j - 1) = sigma(D005940(2^i)) * sigma(D005940(p^j)). Because D005940(1) = 1, and D005940(2n) = 2*D005940(n), the powers of two are among the fixed points of D005940 (cf. J029747), thus the left half of product is sigma(2^i), while on the other hand, we know that D005940(p^j) is odd (because D005940 also preserves parity), and thus the whole product is equal to sigma(2^i * D005940(p^j)) = sigma(D005940(2^i * p^j)) = J324054((2^i * p^j)-1).
